Tire changer helpers are parts of tire changing machines. Tire changers are classified in HTSUS 8505? No. Tire changers are classified in 8428.90 (other lifting, handling machinery) or 8479.89 or 8internal. CBP rulings: tire changers classified under 8487? Actually, tire changing machines are typically classified in 8431? Let me recall: CBP ruling on "tire changers" puts them in 8420? I recall tire changers in 8479.89.9499 (machines having individual functions not specified elsewhere), others 8424.89? I believe tire changers are 8479.89.94. Parts of them are then 8479.90.94 (other parts of machines of 8479).

A ruling for "tire changer helpers" (Models 232, 300, AL32D, Hennessy/Coats) — I think classified in 8479.90.9496 as parts of tire changers. Pneumatic assist arms are parts, so 8479.90.9496.

{"hts_code": "8479.90.9496", "reason": "The assist arms are dedicated parts of tire changing machines, which are classified as machines with individual functions in heading 8479, so they fall under the residual parts provision of subheading 8479.90."}
